    "narrative": "The Austin Waves field a high-upside lineup today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (82.62), who earns the top spot thanks to a favorable matchup against Kumar Rocker. His performance is buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon advantage and a leadoff spot that maximizes his run-scoring potential. Supporting him are **Andy Pages** (75.64) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.13), both of whom capitalize on excellent matchups against Eduardo Rodriguez. **Andy Pages** in particular benefits from a high-efficiency environment where the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts his stolen base probability\u2014a critical factor given our league's focus on speed. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) also projects as a tier-one play, as his matchup against Grant Holmes allows him to lean into a strong 15% skill-based projection boost.\n\nWhile the core is strong, we are managing several \"Lineup Pending\" designations that introduce volatility; we must monitor whether **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** secure their projected batting orders, as their efficiency scores rely heavily on those top-of-the-order opportunities. The most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci**, who posted a 47.36 score. While his leadoff projection and positional flexibility were appealing, he ultimately fell short due to a unfavorable left-on-left platoon disadvantage against Joey Cantillo, pushing him behind the higher-upside profiles of **Nasim Nunez** and **Miguel Vargas**. We are also exercising caution with **Luis Robert Jr.** on the bench today; despite his raw talent, a difficult matchup against Jared Jones and a negative platoon split drop his score to 41.93, falling safely below our start threshold as we prioritize efficiency over reputation to preserve our game caps.",
